  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>Toluene or substituted toluene is converted to benzylidene diacetate on treating with chromic oxide in acetic anhydride. The benzylidene diacetate can be hydrolysed to corresponding benzaldehyde with aqueous acid.</p><p>Chromyl chloride oxidises<br/>methyl group to a chromium complex, which on hydrolysis<br/>gives corresponding benzaldehyde. The reaction is known as Etard reaction.</p><p><img src=\"assets\\st0055_04ab111d6a5c.png\" style=\"width: 600px; height: 271px;\"/></p>"
